<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk"><!--
    ZERO DEPENDENCIES. Not Persistence, not Contracts, not EF Core, not a
    NuGet package. Every reference added here is an architecture change and
    needs a decision-log entry (CLAUDE.md 2.1).

    Domain declares the interfaces; infrastructure implements them.
  -->



  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.SqlServer" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <!--
    The one project allowed to construct a Pseudonym. Its constructor is
    internal so that a call site wanting to write to processing_log has to cross
    the pseudonymisation boundary to obtain the value, which makes CLAUDE.md 4's
    "structural rather than remembered" a compiler rule (decisions.md D-045).

    This grants no reference in the other direction: Domain still depends on
    nothing, and the architecture tests still fail if it acquires anything.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Waymark.Pseudonymisation" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>

